#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2281
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2574
msgid "Venado cola blanca en los claros del bosque"
msgstr "White-tailed deer in the forest clearings"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2284
msgid "Visita a la playa de anidación de tortugas"
msgstr "Visit to the turtle nesting beach"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2285
msgid "Caminata por el sendero costero"
msgstr "Walk along the coastal trail"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2286
msgid "Observación de aves al amanecer"
msgstr "Birdwatching at dawn"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2287
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2329
msgid "Snorkel en el arrecife"
msgstr "Snorkeling on the reef"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2290
msgid "Los senderos son cortos pero rocosos: lleve buen calzado."
msgstr "The trails are short but rocky: wear sturdy footwear."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2291
msgid "No hay servicios en la playa, lleve agua y protector solar."
msgstr "There are no services on the beach, bring water and sunscreen."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2292
msgid "Respete las zonas marcadas de anidación de las tortugas."
msgstr "Respect the marked turtle nesting zones."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2296
msgid "7.800 hectáreas, con el mar y el bosque"
msgstr "7.800 hectares, with the sea and the forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2297
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2633
msgid "1963"
msgstr "1963"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2299
msgid "Bosque seco tropical, costa rocosa y área marina"
msgstr "Tropical dry forest, rocky coast and marine area"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2301
msgid "Junio a noviembre para las tortugas"
msgstr "June to November for turtles"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2302
msgid ""
"Protege el bosque seco y la costa donde anidan tortugas verdes, con áreas "
"delimitadas para su protección."
msgstr ""
"It protects the dry forest and the coast where green turtles nest, with "
"delimited areas set aside for their protection."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2303
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2693
msgid ""
"Se llega por carretera y a pie; los senderos rocosos no admiten sillas de "
"ruedas."
msgstr ""
"Access is by road and on foot; the rocky trails do not accommodate "
"wheelchairs."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2305
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2692
msgid ""
"Cabo Blanco fue declarada reserva absoluta en 1963, la primera del país. Hoy "
"protege unas 7.800 hectáreas de bosque seco, costa rocosa y mar. La playa "
"donde nadaron los Beatles recibe tortugas verdes cada temporada."
msgstr ""
"Cabo Blanco was declared an absolute reserve in 1963, the first in the "
"country. Today it protects some 7.800 hectares of dry forest, rocky coast "
"and sea. The beach where the Beatles swam receives green turtles every "
"season."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2312
msgid ""
"El extremo más norte de la península de Nicoya, con acantilados y bosque "
"seco."
msgstr ""
"The northernmost tip of the Nicoya Peninsula, with cliffs and dry forest."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2314
msgid "Es el punto más septentrional de la península de Nicoya."
msgstr "It is the northernmost point of the Nicoya Peninsula."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2315
msgid "Rodean el cabo el bosque seco y los acantilados rocosos."
msgstr "Dry forest and rocky cliffs surround the cape."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2316
msgid "Desde el mirador se ve todo el Golfo de Papagayo."
msgstr "From the lookout you can see the whole Gulf of Papagayo."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2317
msgid "Cerca están los hoteles y las playas de Playa Nacascolo."
msgstr "The hotels and beaches of Playa Nacascolo are nearby."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2320
msgid "Fragata y pelicano pardo sobre la costa"
msgstr "Frigatebird and brown pelican over the coast"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2323
msgid "Aves playeras en la franja de arena"
msgstr "Shorebirds on the strip of sand"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2326
msgid "Caminata por el sendero costero hasta el acantilado"
msgstr "Walk along the coastal trail to the cliff"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2327
msgid "Paseo en bote por el golfo"
msgstr "Boat ride around the gulf"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2328
msgid "Visita a las playas cercanas"
msgstr "Visit to the nearby beaches"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2332
msgid "El sol es fuerte y no hay sombra en el camino."
msgstr "The sun is strong and there is no shade on the path."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2333
msgid "Los caminos son rocosos, use calzado firme."
msgstr "The paths are rocky, wear sturdy footwear."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2334
msgid "El bosque seco es ralo: no espere sombra."
msgstr "The dry forest is sparse: do not expect shade."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2336
msgid "Acceso libre todo el día en las áreas publicas"
msgstr "Open access all day in the public areas"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2337
msgid "Sin entrada a las playas"
msgstr "No entry fee for the beaches"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2338
msgid "Cabo, Playa Nacascolo y los acantilados del norte"
msgstr "Cape, Playa Nacascolo and the northern cliffs"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2339
msgid "2008"
msgstr "2008"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2341
msgid "Bosque seco tropical, manglar y costa rocosa"
msgstr "Tropical dry forest, mangrove and rocky coast"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2342
msgid "0-80 msnm"
msgstr "0-80 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2344
msgid ""
"El cabo pertenece al Área de Conservación Tempisque, que protege el bosque "
"seco y la anidación de tortugas."
msgstr ""
"The cape belongs to the Tempisque Conservation Area, which protects the dry "
"forest and turtle nesting."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2345
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2698
msgid ""
"Se llega en vehículo por camino de tierra; el sendero al acantilado es de "
"rocas."
msgstr "You arrive by vehicle on a dirt road; the trail to the cliff is rocky."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2347
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2697
msgid ""
"Cabo Papagayo marca el punto más septentrional de la península de Nicoya. El "
"camino costero pasa entre bosque seco y acantilados hasta el mirador del "
"golfo. Alrededor hay hoteles y playas, y al sur el refugio de tortugas de "
"Ostional."
msgstr ""
"Cabo Papagayo marks the northernmost point of the Nicoya Peninsula. The "
"coastal road passes between dry forest and cliffs up to the gulf lookout. "
"Around it there are hotels and beaches, and to the south the Ostional turtle "
"sanctuary."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2354
msgid ""
"El punto más alto de la sierra de Talamanca, con vista al valle de Savegre."
msgstr ""
"The highest point of the Talamanca range, with views over the Savegre Valley."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2356
msgid "Su cima llega a 3.642 msnm y se conoce también como Savegre."
msgstr "Its summit reaches 3.642 masl and is also known as Savegre."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2357
msgid "La carretera interamericana pasa a poca distancia del mirador."
msgstr "The Inter-American Highway passes close to the lookout."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2358
msgid "Desde el mirador se ve el valle de Savegre y el Pacífico."
msgstr "From the lookout you can see the Savegre Valley and the Pacific."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2359
msgid "Alrededor hay plantaciones de pino, páramo y bosque frío de montaña."
msgstr "Around there are pine plantations, páramo and cold montane forest."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2362
msgid "Gallo de monte, ave endémica de la sierra"
msgstr "Wild turkey, endemic bird of the range"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2363
msgid "Quetzal resplandeciente en el bosque nuboso cercano"
msgstr "Resplendent quetzal in the nearby cloud forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2364
msgid "Mono aullador en las zonas más bajas"
msgstr "Howler monkey in the lower areas"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2365
msgid "Tapir de monte, el mamífero mayor del país"
msgstr "Mountain tapir, the largest mammal in the country"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2368
msgid "Caminata por el mirador de la carretera"
msgstr "Walk at the highway lookout"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2369
msgid "Visita a la Reserva Biológica Lomas Barbudal, muy cerca"
msgstr "Visit to Lomas Barbudal Biological Reserve, very close by"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2370
msgid "Recorrido por fincas de café y miel en el valle"
msgstr "Tour of the coffee and honey farms in the valley"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2371
msgid "Fotografía del valle al amanecer"
msgstr "Photography of the valley at dawn"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2374
msgid "Arriba hace frío y viento casi todo el año."
msgstr "It is cold and windy up top almost all year."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2375
msgid "En la mañana hay neblina y la vista se pierde."
msgstr "In the morning there is mist and the view disappears."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2376
msgid "En temporada de lluvias use un vehículo 4x4."
msgstr "In the rainy season use a 4x4 vehicle."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2378
msgid "Acceso todo el día; la carretera permanece abierta todo el año"
msgstr "Open all day; the road stays open all year"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2380
msgid "Mirador y tramo de la ruta 32 en la sierra de Talamanca"
msgstr "Lookout and stretch of Route 32 in the Talamanca range"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2381
msgid "1943"
msgstr "1943"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2382
msgid "Talamanca"
msgstr "Talamanca"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2383
msgid "Páramo de alta altura, bosque de pino y bosque nuboso"
msgstr "High-altitude páramo, pine forest and cloud forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2384
msgid "1.500-3.642 msnm"
msgstr "1.500-3.642 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2385
msgid "Diciembre a abril, y julio para la carretera"
msgstr "December to April, and July for the road"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2386
msgid ""
"Protege el pino, el páramo y el bosque nuboso de la sierra de Talamanca."
msgstr ""
"It protects the pine trees, the páramo and the cloud forest of the Talamanca "
"range."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2387
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2703
msgid "Llega en vehículo por la ruta 32; el mirador no tiene rampa."
msgstr "Get there by vehicle on Route 32; the lookout has no ramp."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2389
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2702
msgid ""
"A 3.642 msnm está la cima más alta de la sierra de Talamanca. La carretera "
"interamericana que cruza el cerro se completó en 1943. Desde el mirador se "
"ve el valle de Savegre y el mar en días claros."
msgstr ""
"At 3.642 masl lies the highest summit of the Talamanca range. The Inter-"
"American Highway crossing the mountain was completed in 1943. From the "
"lookout you can see the Savegre Valley and the sea on clear days."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2396
msgid ""
"La península más grande del país: bosque seco al norte y selva húmeda al sur."
msgstr ""
"The largest peninsula in the country: dry forest in the north and rainforest "
"in the south."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2398
msgid "La península mide unos 3.200 km² y es la más grande del país."
msgstr "The peninsula covers some 3.200 km² and is the largest in the country."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2399
msgid "El norte es bosque seco y el sur es selva húmeda."
msgstr "The north is dry forest and the south is rainforest."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2400
msgid "El Área de Conservación Guanacaste fue creada en 1991."
msgstr "The Guanacaste Conservation Area was created in 1991."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2401
msgid "Allí están Santa Rosa, Palo Verde y el río Tempisque."
msgstr "Santa Rosa, Palo Verde and the Tempisque River are located there."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2404
msgid "Venado cola blanca en el bosque seco"
msgstr "White-tailed deer in the dry forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2405
msgid "Mono aullador en la selva del sur"
msgstr "Howler monkey in the southern rainforest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2406
msgid "Tortuga verde en las playas del Golfo de Nicoya"
msgstr "Green turtle on the beaches of the Gulf of Nicoya"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2407
msgid "Ara escarlata en los árboles del bosque seco"
msgstr "Scarlet macaw in the dry forest trees"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2410
msgid "Visita a las áreas protegidas de la península"
msgstr "Visit to the protected areas of the peninsula"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2411
msgid "Paseo en bote por el río Tempisque"
msgstr "Boat ride along the Tempisque River"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2412
msgid "Visita a los pueblos pesqueros del sur"
msgstr "Visit to the southern fishing towns"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2413
msgid "Recorrido por el cabo y sus miradores"
msgstr "Tour of the cape and its lookouts"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2416
msgid "Las distancias entre los extremos de la península son largas."
msgstr "Distances between the ends of the peninsula are long."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2417
msgid "El sur es muy lluvioso en temporada."
msgstr "The south is very rainy in season."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2418
msgid "Planifique la ruta con un mapa antes de salir."
msgstr "Plan your route with a map before setting out."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2420
msgid "Acceso libre todo el día; cada reserva cobra su entrada"
msgstr "Open access all day; each reserve charges its own fee"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2421
msgid "Sin entrada general; cada reserva protegida tiene la suya"
msgstr "No general entry fee; each protected reserve has its own"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2422
msgid "Península de 3.200 km² con áreas protegidas de todo tipo"
msgstr "A 3.200 km² peninsula with protected areas of every kind"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2425
msgid "Del bosque seco tropical a la selva húmeda"
msgstr "From tropical dry forest to rainforest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2426
msgid "0-1.200 msnm"
msgstr "0-1.200 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2427
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2469
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2511
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2553
msgid "Diciembre a abril"
msgstr "December to April"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2428
msgid ""
"El Área de Conservación Guanacaste protege un mosaico de bosque seco, "
"humedales y costa."
msgstr ""
"The Guanacaste Conservation Area protects a mosaic of dry forest, wetlands "
"and coast."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2429
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2708
msgid "Se recorre en vehículo 4x4; los senderos de cada reserva son de tierra."
msgstr "It is explored by 4x4 vehicle; the trails in each reserve are dirt."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2430
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2709
msgid "https://whc.UNESCO.org/en/list/928/"
msgstr "https://whc.UNESCO.org/en/list/928/"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2431
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2707
msgid ""
"La península de Nicoya es la mayor del país, con 3.200 km². Al norte el "
"bosque seco, al sur la selva húmeda y el Osa. El Área de Conservación "
"Guanacaste, creada en 1991, protege el norte de la península."
msgstr ""
"The Nicoya Peninsula is the largest in the country, at 3.200 km². To the "
"north, dry forest; to the south, rainforest and the Osa. The Guanacaste "
"Conservation Area, created in 1991, protects the northern part of the "
"peninsula."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2438
msgid ""
"La mayor selva primaria de las montanas centrales, con un río que la "
"atraviesa."
msgstr ""
"The largest primary forest in the central mountains, with a river running "
"through it."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2440
msgid ""
"Creado en 1978, protege la mayor selva primaria de las montanas centrales."
msgstr ""
"Created in 1978, it protects the largest primary forest in the central "
"mountains."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2441
msgid "Un solo sector del parque está abierto a los visitantes."
msgstr "Only one sector of the park is open to visitors."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2442
msgid "De 42.000 hectáreas, solo una parte pequeña recibe visitas."
msgstr "Of 42.000 hectares, only a small part receives visitors."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2443
msgid "El río Braulio Carrillo cruza el parque de lado a lado."
msgstr "The Braulio Carrillo River runs across the park from side to side."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2446
msgid "La harpía, ave de rapaz mayor, sobrevuela el dosel"
msgstr "The harpy eagle, the largest raptor, soars over the canopy"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2447
msgid "Ocelote y oso de anteojos en el suelo del bosque"
msgstr "Ocelot and spectacled bear on the forest floor"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2448
msgid "Mono aullador y perezoso de dos dedos"
msgstr "Howler monkey and two-toed sloth"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2449
msgid "Tucanes y pavas en el bosque de ribera"
msgstr "Toucans and peafowl in the riparian forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2452
msgid "Caminata guiada por el sendero del río Braulio Carrillo"
msgstr "Guided walk along the Braulio Carrillo River trail"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2453
msgid "Observación de aves con guía especialista"
msgstr "Birdwatching with a specialist guide"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2454
msgid "Visita al centro de interpretación del parque"
msgstr "Visit to the park's interpretation center"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2455
msgid "Baño en la cascada y la poza natural"
msgstr "Swim at the waterfall and the natural pool"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2458
msgid "Use manga larga: el bosque es denso y con mosquitos."
msgstr "Wear long sleeves: the forest is dense and full of mosquitoes."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2459
msgid "El sendero es resbaloso cuando hay humedad."
msgstr "The trail is slippery when damp."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2460
msgid "No entre al río: la corriente es fuerte."
msgstr "Do not enter the river: the current is strong."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2464
msgid "42.000 hectáreas"
msgstr "42,000 hectares"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2465
msgid "1978"
msgstr "1978"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2466
msgid "Huetar Norte"
msgstr "North Huetar"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2467
msgid "Bosque húmedo tropical y cerros karsticos"
msgstr "Tropical rainforest and karst hills"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2468
msgid "60-1.174 msnm"
msgstr "60-1,174 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2470
msgid ""
"Conserva la mayor mancha de selva primaria de las montanas centrales del "
"país."
msgstr ""
"It preserves the largest patch of primary forest in the country's central "
"mountains."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2471
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2713
msgid ""
"Los senderos son de tierra, con pendientes y raíces; no hay acceso en silla "
"de ruedas."
msgstr ""
"The trails are dirt paths, with slopes and roots; there is no wheelchair "
"access."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2473
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2712
msgid ""
"El parque protege una de las últimas manchas grandes de selva primaria del "
"país. El río Braulio Carrillo lo atraviesa y define el sector abierto a "
"visitas. El bosque conserva especies raras como la harpía y el ocelote."
msgstr ""
"The park protects one of the last large patches of primary forest in the "
"country. The Braulio Carrillo River runs through it and defines the sector "
"open to visitors. The forest holds rare species such as the harpy eagle and "
"the ocelot."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2480
msgid ""
"Bosque nuboso de las montañas volcánicas centrales con una gran población de "
"quetzal."
msgstr ""
"Cloud forest of the central volcanic mountains with a large quetzal "
"population."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2482
msgid ""
"Creado en 1982, protege el bosque más extenso de la sierra volcánica central."
msgstr ""
"Created in 1982, it protects the largest forest in the central volcanic "
"range."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2483
msgid "Su bosque de neblina alberga una de las mayores poblaciones de quetzal."
msgstr "Its cloud forest harbors one of the largest quetzal populations."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2484
msgid "El Mirador de la Gollita mira al valle y al dosel del bosque."
msgstr "Mirador de la Gollita looks out over the valley and the forest canopy."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2485
msgid "El Sendero del Quetzal une el parque con el valle de Savegre."
msgstr "The Quetzal Trail links the park with the Savegre Valley."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2488
msgid "Quetzal resplandeciente, la estrella del parque"
msgstr "Resplendent quetzal, the star of the park"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2489
msgid "Momoto resplandeciente en el dosel del bosque"
msgstr "Resplendent motmot in the forest canopy"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2490
msgid "Aves de seda y colibríes de la neblina"
msgstr "Silky flycatchers and cloud forest hummingbirds"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2491
msgid "Mono aullador y tapir de monte en el sotobosque"
msgstr "Howler monkey and tapir in the understory"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2494
msgid "Observación de quetzal con guía en el mirador"
msgstr "Guided quetzal watching at the viewpoint"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2495
msgid "Caminata por los senderos de la reserva"
msgstr "Walk along the reserve trails"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2496
msgid "Observación de aves en el Mirador de la Gollita"
msgstr "Birdwatching at Mirador de la Gollita"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2497
msgid "Visita a una finca de café en los alrededores"
msgstr "Visit to a coffee farm in the surrounding area"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2500
msgid "El sendero al mirador del quetzal es fangoso y resbaloso."
msgstr "The trail to the quetzal viewpoint is muddy and slippery."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2501
msgid "Lleve agua y bocadillos: no hay servicios dentro."
msgstr "Bring water and snacks: there are no services inside."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2502
msgid "La puerta cierra a las 15:00, no después."
msgstr "The gate closes at 15:00, not later."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2505
msgid "Entrada: $5 extranjeros / 1.000 colones nacionales"
msgstr "Entry: $5 for foreigners / 1,000 colones for nationals"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2506
msgid "9.500 hectáreas"
msgstr "9,500 hectares"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2507
msgid "1982"
msgstr "1982"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2508
msgid "Cartago"
msgstr "Cartago"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2509
msgid "Bosque nuboso húmedo de la sierra volcánica central"
msgstr "Humid cloud forest of the central volcanic range"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2510
msgid "1.600-2.600 msnm"
msgstr "1,600-2,600 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2512
msgid ""
"Sostiene al quetzal y protege el bosque nuboso más extenso de la sierra "
"volcánica central."
msgstr ""
"It sustains the quetzal and protects the largest cloud forest in the central "
"volcanic range."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2513
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2718
msgid ""
"Los senderos son de tierra, con barro y pendientes; no hay acceso en silla "
"de ruedas."
msgstr ""
"The trails are dirt paths, with mud and slopes; there is no wheelchair "
"access."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2515
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2717
msgid ""
"Tapantial protege el bosque nuboso más extenso de la sierra volcánica "
"central. El quetzal anida en el dosel y se observa con guía desde el "
"mirador. A las 15:00 cierra la puerta y el valle queda en silencio."
msgstr ""
"Tapantial protects the largest cloud forest in the central volcanic range. "
"The quetzal nests in the canopy and is seen with a guide from the viewpoint. "
"At 15:00 the gate closes and the valley falls silent."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2522
msgid ""
"El último gran tramo de bosque seco del Pacífico central, con el río "
"Tárcoles."
msgstr ""
"The last large stretch of dry forest in the central Pacific, with the "
"Tárcoles River."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2524
msgid ""
"Creado en 1995, protege la mayor extensión de bosque seco del Pacífico "
"central."
msgstr ""
"Created in 1995, it protects the largest area of dry forest in the central "
"Pacific."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2525
msgid "El río Tárcoles marca el límite norte del área protegida."
msgstr "The Tárcoles River marks the northern boundary of the protected area."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2526
msgid "El mirador de la Piedra Bola domina la selva y el valle."
msgstr "The Piedra Bola viewpoint overlooks the forest and the valley."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2527
msgid "Los manglares del estero son parte de la zona protegida."
msgstr "The estuary mangroves are part of the protected area."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2530
msgid "Ara escarlata en parejas y bandadas del bosque seco"
msgstr "Scarlet macaws in pairs and dry forest flocks"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2531
msgid "Capuchin de cara blanca en los árboles del bosque"
msgstr "White-faced capuchins in the forest trees"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2532
msgid "Puma que recorre el parque de madrugada"
msgstr "Puma roaming the park at dawn"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2533
msgid "Crocodrilos del río Tárcoles en las barras de arena"
msgstr "Crocodiles of the Tárcoles River on the sandbars"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2536
msgid "Caminata hasta el mirador de la Piedra Bola"
msgstr "Walk to the Piedra Bola viewpoint"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2537
msgid "Observación de aves a lo largo del río Tárcoles"
msgstr "Birdwatching along the Tárcoles River"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2538
msgid "Paseo en bote por el estero y los manglares"
msgstr "Boat ride through the estuary and the mangroves"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2539
msgid "Visita a una granja de crocodilos"
msgstr "Visit to a crocodile farm"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2542
msgid "El último tramo del río solo se recorre en bote."
msgstr "The last stretch of the river can only be explored by boat."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2543
msgid "El camino de entrada es de tierra y grava."
msgstr "The access road is dirt and gravel."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2544
msgid "Lleve repelente: en temporada hay muchos mosquitos."
msgstr "Bring insect repellent: in season there are many mosquitoes."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2548
msgid "11.700 hectáreas"
msgstr "11,700 hectares"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2550
msgid "Alajuela"
msgstr "Alajuela"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2551
msgid "Bosque seco tropical y manglares del Pacífico central"
msgstr "Tropical dry forest and mangroves of the central Pacific"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2552
msgid "0-400 msnm"
msgstr "0-400 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2554
msgid ""
"Salva el último tramo de bosque seco del Pacífico central y protege los "
"manglares."
msgstr ""
"It saves the last stretch of dry forest in the central Pacific and protects "
"the mangroves."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2555
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2723
msgid ""
"El mirador se alcanza por sendero de tierra; el estero solo se visita en "
"bote."
msgstr ""
"The viewpoint is reached by a dirt trail; the estuary is only visited by "
"boat."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2557
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2722
msgid ""
"El parque protege el bosque seco que quedó entre el río Tárcoles y el "
"Pacífico. El mirador de la Piedra Bola ofrece la mejor vista del sector. El "
"río y los manglares se recorren en bote desde la entrada principal."
msgstr ""
"The park protects the dry forest left between the Tárcoles River and the "
"Pacific. The Piedra Bola viewpoint offers the best view of the area. The "
"river and the mangroves are explored by boat from the main entrance."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2564
msgid ""
"Pueblo de surf con una playa protegida por el proyecto de tortugas Ostional."
msgstr "Surf town with a beach protected by the Ostional turtle project."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2566
msgid "Pueblo de surf en la península de Nicoya, al norte de Guanacaste."
msgstr "Surf town on the Nicoya Peninsula, north of Guanacaste."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2567
msgid "Su playa de unos 1,4 km va del río Samara hasta el mar."
msgstr "Its 1.4 km beach runs from the Samara River to the sea."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2568
msgid "El estuario entre el Womble y el río atrae cientos de aves."
msgstr ""
"The estuary between the Womble and the river attracts hundreds of birds."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2569
msgid "Cerca están Isla Chora y la finca Rancho Quemado, con tortugas."
msgstr "Nearby are Isla Chora and the Rancho Quemado farm, with turtles."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2572
msgid "Tortuga verde anidando en la arena de la playa"
msgstr "Green turtle nesting in the beach sand"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2573
msgid "Mono aullador en el bosque seco cercano"
msgstr "Howler monkey in the nearby dry forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2575
msgid "Ara en los árboles del bosque seco"
msgstr "Macaw in the dry forest trees"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2578
msgid "Caminar por la playa durante la marea baja"
msgstr "Walk along the beach at low tide"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2579
msgid "Observación de aves en el estuario del río"
msgstr "Birdwatching at the river estuary"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2580
msgid "Recorrido de anidación de tortugas en Rancho Quemado"
msgstr "Turtle nesting tour at Rancho Quemado"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2581
msgid "Clase de surf para principiantes"
msgstr "Beginner surf lesson"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2584
msgid "La boca del río no es segura para nadar."
msgstr "The river mouth is not safe for swimming."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2585
msgid "La playa tiene corrientes fuertes y resacas."
msgstr "The beach has strong currents and rip tides."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2586
msgid "No deje sus pertenencias sobre la arena."
msgstr "Do not leave your belongings on the sand."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2588
msgid "Abierto todo el día"
msgstr "Open all day"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2589
msgid ""
"Sin entrada para la playa; el recorrido de tortugas tiene su propio precio"
msgstr "No beach entry fee; the turtle tour has its own price"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2590
msgid "Sector Ostional con unas 3.000 ha de playa y 2.700 ha marinas"
msgstr ""
"Ostional sector with about 3,000 ha of beach and 2,700 ha of marine waters"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2593
msgid "Bosque seco tropical, estuario de río y playa arenosa"
msgstr "Tropical dry forest, river estuary and sandy beach"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2594
msgid "0-30 msnm"
msgstr "0-30 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2596
msgid ""
"La playa protege los sitios de anidación de tortugas verdes dentro del "
"proyecto Ostional."
msgstr ""
"The beach protects the green turtle nesting sites within the Ostional "
"project."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2597
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2728
msgid ""
"Se llega en bus o auto por carretera; la arena firme permite acceso a pie."
msgstr ""
"It is reached by bus or car by road; the firm sand allows access on foot."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2599
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2727
msgid ""
"Samara es un pueblo de surf en la península de Nicoya con playa de 1,4 km. "
"La entrada del río Samara forma un estuario con gran variedad de aves. La "
"playa forma parte del proyecto de tortugas Ostional."
msgstr ""
"Samara is a surf town on the Nicoya Peninsula with a 1.4 km beach. The mouth "
"of the Samara River forms an estuary with a wide variety of birds. The beach "
"is part of the Ostional turtle project."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2606
msgid "Puerto de entrada a la península de Osa y al parque nacional Corcovado."
msgstr "Gateway port to the Osa Peninsula and Corcovado National Park."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2608
msgid "Principal puerto de acceso a la península de Osa y al parque Corcovado."
msgstr "Main access port to the Osa Peninsula and Corcovado National Park."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2609
msgid "El pueblo se desarrollo con la creación del parque en 1963."
msgstr "The town grew with the creation of the park in 1963."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2610
msgid "La entrada principal del parque está a unos 10 km del centro."
msgstr "The main park entrance is about 10 km from the center."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2611
msgid "Hoy es la base de una gran cantidad de lodges de aventura."
msgstr "Today it is the base for a large number of adventure lodges."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2614
msgid "Ara escarlata en el dosel de la selva"
msgstr "Scarlet macaw in the rainforest canopy"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2615
msgid "Mono aullador en el bosque húmedo"
msgstr "Howler monkey in the humid forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2616
msgid "Tapir en los senderos del parque"
msgstr "Tapir on the park trails"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2617
msgid "Martin pescador a orillas del río Agujas"
msgstr "Kingfisher on the banks of the Agujas River"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2620
msgid "Visita al parque nacional Corcovado"
msgstr "Visit to Corcovado National Park"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2621
msgid "Paseo en bote por la Bahía de Drake"
msgstr "Boat ride through Drake Bay"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2622
msgid "Caminata sobre el manglar en Playa Juan Castillo"
msgstr "Walk on the mangroves at Playa Juan Castillo"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2623
msgid "Visita a los lodges de la zona"
msgstr "Visit to the lodges in the area"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2626
msgid "El camino al parque es de tierra y queda en mal estado."
msgstr "The road to the park is dirt and in poor condition."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2627
msgid "Reserve el permiso del parque y el guía con antelación."
msgstr "Book the park permit and guide in advance."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2628
msgid "Lleve efectivo porque hay pocos cajeros."
msgstr "Bring cash because there are few ATMs."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2630
msgid "Todo el día; los cupos del parque se reservan con antelación"
msgstr "All day; park quotas are booked in advance"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2631
msgid "Sin entrada al pueblo; Corcovado exige permiso, guía y pago"
msgstr ""
"No fee to enter the town; Corcovado requires a permit, guide and payment"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2632
msgid "Pueblo costero con lodges, al norte de la península de Osa"
msgstr "Coastal town with lodges, north of the Osa Peninsula"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2635
msgid "Selva tropical húmeda y manglar costero"
msgstr "Humid tropical rainforest and coastal mangrove"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2636
msgid "0-50 msnm"
msgstr "0-50 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2638
msgid ""
"Corcovado protege el bosque tropical húmedo más extenso del país y la vida "
"marina de Osa."
msgstr ""
"Corcovado protects the country's largest humid tropical forest and the "
"marine life of Osa."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2639
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2733
msgid ""
"El pueblo tiene calle principal pavimentada; el camino al parque es de "
"tierra y exige 4x4."
msgstr ""
"The town has a paved main street; the road to the park is dirt and requires "
"a 4x4."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2641
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2732
msgid ""
"Puerto Jimenez es la principal puerta de entrada a la península de Osa. El "
"parque nacional Corcovado está a unos 10 km del pueblo. Al sur comienza la "
"Bahía de Drake y su reserva marina."
msgstr ""
"Puerto Jimenez is the main gateway to the Osa Peninsula. Corcovado National "
"Park is about 10 km from the town. To the south begins Drake Bay and its "
"marine reserve."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2737
msgid ""
"El Arenal es un estratovolcan de 1.670 msnm en el norte de Costa Rica. "
"Erupciono entre 1968 y 2010, con flujos de lava que brillaban de noche. La "
"colada de 1968 es hoy un sendero. El Observatorio Arenal está en la "
"carretera de subida."
msgstr ""
"Arenal is a 1,670 masl stratovolcano in northern Costa Rica. It erupted "
"between 1968 and 2010, with lava flows that glowed at night. The 1968 flow "
"is now a trail. Arenal Observatory is on the road up."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2738
msgid ""
"Se llega en vehículo hasta el mirador. El cráter se visita en vehículo "
"abierto. El clima es caluroso en la base."
msgstr ""
"You can drive as far as the viewpoint. The crater is visited in an open "
"vehicle. It is hot at the base."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2742
msgid ""
"Tortuguero es un parque de selva húmeda en la costa del Caribe. Solo se "
"llega en bote o en avión. Sus 31.187 hectáreas están cruzadas por canales y "
"el pueblo no tiene carreteras. Guarda la mayor playa de desove de tortuga "
"verde del hemisferio, de julio a octubre."
msgstr ""
"Tortuguero is a rainforest park on the Caribbean coast. It can only be "
"reached by boat or plane. Its 31,187 hectares are crisscrossed by canals and "
"the village has no roads. It holds the hemisphere's largest green turtle "
"nesting beach, from July to October."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2743
msgid ""
"No hay acceso por tierra: todo el recorrido es en bote y solo con guía. El "
"pueblo es plano pero la humedad es alta."
msgstr ""
"There is no road access: the whole route is by boat and only with a guide. "
"The village is flat but the humidity is high."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2747
msgid ""
"Manuel Antonio es el parque más visitado de Costa Rica. Es uno de los más "
"pequenos, con 1.983 hectáreas. Sus tres playas son Espadilla Sur, Manuel "
"Antonio y Puerto Escondido. Los monos carablanca y titi se ven en los "
"senderos y el parque cierra los lunes."
msgstr ""
"Manuel Antonio is the most visited park in Costa Rica. It is one of the "
"smallest, with 1,983 hectares. Its three beaches are Espadilla Sur, Manuel "
"Antonio and Puerto Escondido. White-faced capuchins and titi monkeys are "
"seen on the trails, and the park closes on Mondays."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2748
msgid ""
"Las playas son de arena y hay escalones en los accesos. El parque es "
"transitable a pie, pero con mucha gente."
msgstr ""
"The beaches are sandy and there are steps at the entrances. The park can be "
"walked, but it gets crowded."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2752
msgid ""
"Corcovado protege el mayor bosque primario que queda en el Pacífico de "
"Mesoamerica. Cubre 42.469 hectáreas. Reune las cuatro especies de monos del "
"país, junto con tapir, jaguar y puma. El ingreso es obligatorio con guía. Se "
"hace por las estaciones de Los Patos y Sirena."
msgstr ""
"Corcovado protects the largest primary forest left in Mesoamerica's Pacific. "
"It covers 42,469 hectares. It brings together the country's four monkey "
"species, along with tapir, jaguar and puma. A guide is mandatory. Entry is "
"through the Los Patos and Sirena ranger stations."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2753
msgid ""
"El acceso es en bote o a pie por senderos de tierra. El clima es caluroso y "
"húmedo todo el año."
msgstr ""
"Access is by boat or on foot along dirt trails. The climate is hot and humid "
"year round."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2757
msgid ""
"Rincón de la Vieja tiene nueve conos volcanicos. El Von Seebach es el más "
"alto, con 1.895 msnm. Fumarolas, ollas de barro hirviendo y la catarata La "
"Cangreja llenan el sector norte. Las termas del Río Clarillo son parte del "
"Área de Conservación Guanacaste. Es Patrimonio de la Humanidad de la UNESCO."
msgstr ""
"Rincón de la Vieja has nine volcanic cones. Von Seebach is the tallest, at "
"1,895 masl. Fumaroles, boiling mud pots and La Cangreja waterfall fill the "
"northern sector. The Río Clarillo hot springs are part of the Guanacaste "
"Conservation Area. It is a UNESCO World Heritage Site."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2758
msgid ""
"El sendero a la catarata es de tierra y se llega en vehículo. Las termas "
"tienen plataformas de descanso."
msgstr ""
"The trail to the waterfall is dirt and you can reach it by vehicle. The hot "
"springs have rest platforms."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2762
msgid ""
"Poás tiene uno de los crateres volcanicos más anchos del mundo. Su diametro "
"es de 1,3 km. La laguna del cráter cambia de color. La cima está a un corto "
"sendero desde el estacionamiento. Los gases son toxicos, por eso hay "
"barreras, y la visita exige reserva por turno."
msgstr ""
"Poás has one of the widest volcanic craters in the world. Its diameter is "
"1.3 km. The crater lagoon changes color. The summit is a short walk from the "
"parking lot. The gases are toxic, so there are barriers, and visits require "
"a timed reservation."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2763
msgid ""
"El mirador se alcanza sin esfuerzo. Hace frío y hay que subir de vuelta en "
"vehículo por la altura."
msgstr ""
"The viewpoint is reached with no effort. It is cold, and you have to drive "
"back up because of the altitude."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2767
msgid ""
"Irazú es el volcán más alto de Costa Rica, con 3.432 msnm. En días "
"despejados se ven los dos oceanos. La laguna del cráter cambia de color con "
"los minerales. La carretera llega cerca del cráter. La cima es fría y "
"ventosa todo el año."
msgstr ""
"Irazú is the tallest volcano in Costa Rica, at 3,432 masl. On clear days you "
"can see both oceans. The crater lagoon changes color with the minerals. The "
"road reaches close to the crater. The summit is cold and windy year round."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2768
msgid ""
"La carretera llega casi al cráter sin caminata. El frío y el viento hacen "
"que conviene bajar pronto."
msgstr ""
"The road reaches almost to the crater with no walking. The cold and wind "
"make it wise to head back down early."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2772
msgid ""
"Chirripó es el punto más alto de Costa Rica, con 3.820 msnm. Sus lagos "
"glaciares Ditkevi y Chadolin son la principal atracción. El amanecer sobre "
"el Pacífico completa el paisaje. El páramo está cubierto de frailejones y el "
"refugio se debe reservar con anticipacion."
msgstr ""
"Chirripó is the highest point in Costa Rica, at 3,820 masl. Its glacial "
"lakes Ditkevi and Chadolin are the main attraction. Sunrise over the Pacific "
"completes the landscape. The páramo is covered with frailejones and the "
"refuge must be booked in advance."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2773
msgid ""
"La subida toma dos días y el clima cambia muy rápido. Hace falta refugiarse "
"y llevar ropa de frío."
msgstr ""
"The climb takes two days and the weather changes very fast. You need to take "
"shelter and bring warm clothing."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2777
msgid ""
"Cahuita protege un arrecife de coral, una playa y un bosque de manglar. El "
"terremoto de 1991 levantó la costa y formo la playa actual. El arrecife está "
"bien conservado para el snorkel y un sendero de 8 km une la playa y el "
"bosque."
msgstr ""
"Cahuita protects a coral reef, a beach and a mangrove forest. The 1991 "
"earthquake uplifted the coast and formed the present beach. The reef is well "
"preserved for snorkeling, and an 8 km trail links the beach and the forest."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2778
msgid ""
"El sendero es de tierra y de tramo corto; el mar tiene corrientes y no hay "
"servicios dentro del parque."
msgstr ""
"The trail is a short dirt path; the sea has currents and there are no "
"services inside the park."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2782
msgid ""
"Marino Ballena protege 5.375 hectáreas, casi todas marinas, alrededor de la "
"península de Osa. Su tormbolo de arena parece una cola de ballena en marea "
"baja. Ballenas jorobadas de los dos hemisferios migran aqui y Uvita organiza "
"el festival de la ballena en temporada."
msgstr ""
"Marino Ballena protects 5,375 hectares, almost all of them marine, around "
"the Osa Peninsula. Its sandbar looks like a whale's tail at low tide. "
"Humpback whales from both hemispheres migrate here, and Uvita hosts the "
"whale festival in season."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2783
msgid ""
"El avistamiento se hace en lancha y el tormbolo se recorre a pie; no hay "
"acceso en silla de ruedas."
msgstr ""
"Whale watching is done by motorboat and the sandbar is walked on foot; there "
"is no wheelchair access."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2787
msgid ""
"Guayabo fue la ciudad precolombina más importante de Costa Rica, habitada "
"entre el 1000 a.C. y el 1400 d.C. Sus acueductos y tanques de piedra siguen "
"funcionando y las calzadas empedradas conectan los monticulos. Fue declarado "
"monumento nacional en 1973 y patrimonio de la ingenieria en 2009."
msgstr ""
"Guayabo was the most important pre-Columbian city in Costa Rica, inhabited "
"between 1000 BC and 1400 AD. Its aqueducts and stone tanks still work, and "
"the paved causeways connect the mounds. It was declared a national monument "
"in 1973 and a UNESCO engineering World Heritage Site in 2009."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2788
msgid ""
"El sendero principal es de tierra y es accesible en silla de ruedas; el "
"museo está a corta distancia."
msgstr ""
"The main trail is dirt and wheelchair accessible; the museum is a short "
"distance away."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2789
msgid "https://www.museosycostarica.go.cr/"
msgstr "https://www.museosycostarica.go.cr/"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2792
msgid ""
"Tenorio tiene cuatro volcánes apagados y bosque nuboso con tapires y "
"quetzales. El Río Celeste se vuelve turquesa donde se mezclan dos ríos, "
"dentro del Área de Conservación Guanacaste. Un sendero de 3 km lleva a la "
"laguna azul, los tenideros y la catarata."
msgstr ""
"Tenorio has four dormant volcanoes and cloud forest with tapirs and "
"quetzals. The Río Celeste turns turquoise where two rivers meet, within the "
"Guanacaste Conservation Area. A 3 km trail leads to the blue lagoon, the "
"swimming pools and the waterfall."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2793
msgid ""
"El sendero es de tierra y empedrado con pendientes; hay que caminar entre "
"tres y cinco horas."
msgstr ""
"The trail is dirt and cobbled, with slopes; the walk takes between three and "
"five hours."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2797
msgid ""
"Palo Verde protege el humedal más importante de Costa Rica. Miles de aves "
"acuáticas migratorias, entre ellas los jabiru, pasan el invierno en sus "
"lagunas. Hay cocodrilos en las lagunas y el parque conserva uno de los "
"últimos bosques tropicales secos del país."
msgstr ""
"Palo Verde protects the most important wetland in Costa Rica. Thousands of "
"migratory waterbirds, including jabirus, spend the winter in its lagoons. "
"There are crocodiles in the lagoons and the park preserves one of the last "
"tropical dry forests in the country."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2798
msgid ""
"El recorrido principal es en lancha por las lagunas; el centro de visitantes "
"es accesible a pie."
msgstr ""
"The main tour is by motorboat through the lagoons; the visitor center is "
"accessible on foot."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2799
msgid "https://www.acguanacaste.ac.cr/"
msgstr "https://www.acguanacaste.ac.cr/"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2802
msgid ""
"Isla del Coco está a 550 km de la costa y es Patrimonio de la Humanidad de "
"la UNESCO desde 1997. Concentra más de 400 especies endémicas de insectos y "
"plantas, ademas de cardumenes estacionales de tiburones martillo. El permiso "
"de acceso lo emite el parque."
msgstr ""
"Isla del Coco is 550 km off the coast and has been a UNESCO World Heritage "
"Site since 1997. It holds more than 400 endemic insect and plant species, "
"plus seasonal schools of hammerhead sharks. The park issues the access "
"permit."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2803
msgid ""
"Solo se llega en barco, con 36 horas de viaje; no hay ninguna facilidad en "
"la isla."
msgstr ""
"You can only get there by boat, with a 36-hour journey; the island has no "
"facilities at all."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2807
msgid ""
"Gandoca-Manzanillo protege manglares, un arrecife de coral y una playa de "
"arena de desove. La playa es sitio de anidación de tortuga baula, una de las "
"últimas poblaciones del Caribe. Un sendero costero une Manzanillo con la "
"laguna de Gandoca entre bosque de cativo y mangle rojo."
msgstr ""
"Gandoca-Manzanillo protects mangroves, a coral reef and a nesting beach. The "
"beach is a nesting site for the hawksbill turtle, one of the last "
"populations in the Caribbean. A coastal trail links Manzanillo with the "
"Gandoca lagoon through cativo forest and red mangrove."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2808
msgid ""
"El sendero costero es de tierra y de clima caluroso; la playa es de arena "
"blanda y no tiene servicios."
msgstr ""
"The coastal trail is dirt and the climate is hot; the beach is soft sand and "
"has no services."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2911
msgid "Todavía no hay fotografías acreditadas."
msgstr "No credited photographs yet."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2913
msgid ""
"Las fotografías de los destinos proceden de Wikimedia Commons y se usan bajo "
"las licencias indicadas. Los créditos se muestran también en cada ficha y en "
"el mapa interactivo."
msgstr ""
"Destination photos come from Wikimedia Commons and are used under the "
"licenses shown. Credits are also displayed on each destination page and in "
"the interactive map."

